  "reasoning": "The claim misrepresents the findings of a widely cited March 2023 report by Goldman Sachs economists (Hatzius et al.). The report did not predict that generative AI \"will replace\" 300 million jobs. Rather, it estimated that generative AI could expose the equivalent of roughly 300 million full-time jobs globally to automation. \n\nCrucially, the authors distinguished between tasks being automated and workers being replaced. The report noted that for most workers, AI would serve as a complement rather than a substitute, partially automating tasks while enhancing overall productivity. Transforming an economic estimate of potential task exposure into a definitive prediction of 300 million job losses exaggerates and distorts the source's actual conclusions.",
